// Sheet: "summon a churning storm cloud overhead... while the cloud lingers
// you can call down another bolt each round" -- a persistent zone the caster
// manually re-triggers every round. No engine primitive lets a spell recast
// itself for free on a timer, and no lingering-cloud entity exists
// independent of an actual strike -- ships as a single GroundAoe lightning
// strike (the same "keep the damage burst, drop the persistence/repeat
// rider" simplification create_bonfire.ron/dust_devil.ron already use); a
// player who wants another bolt simply recasts the spell at its energy cost,
// which is the closest in-engine equivalent to "call down another bolt".
// `GroundAoe`'s damage strike is hardcoded to `DamageKind::Energy` -- the
// sheet's Lightning damage_type is flavor-only, same pre-existing gap every
// GroundAoe spell in this pipeline ships with. Radius uses the sheet's own
// per-bolt strike footprint (Sphere r1.5), not the much larger ~30 m
// storm-cloud flavor text, since only the strike itself is mechanically
// real.
GroundAoe(
    energy_cost: 95.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.65,
    delay: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    max_range: 37.0,
    radius: 1.5,
    min_falloff: 0.5,
    damage: 36.0,
    poise: 15.0,
    knockback: (strength: 0.0, direction: Away),
    dodgeable: Roll,
    reagent: Some(Yellow),
    rooted_cast: false,
    meta: (school: Some(Conjuration), source: Some(Primordial)),
)
